<header><p class="st-kicker">county · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Nice</h1><p class="st-meta">1388 CE – 1860 CE · capital Nice</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Riviera county that chose Savoy over Provence in 1388, gave the Savoyards their outlet to the sea and passed to France in 1860.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the war of succession that followed Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joanna-i-of-naples">Joanna I</a>'s death, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a> and its hinterland rejected the Angevin claimant and in 1388, in the act known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dedition-of-nice-to-savoy">Dedition</a>, placed themselves under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-vii-count-of-savoy">Amadeus VII of Savoy</a>. Nice thus left the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-provence">County of Provence</a> and became Savoy's outlet to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The county was governed by Savoyard officials and later a senate at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/villefranche-sur-mer">Villefranche</a> as the dukes' naval base. In 1543 a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-ottoman-alliance">Franco-Ottoman</a> fleet besieged Nice, an event remembered through the heroine Catherine Ségurane. The people spoke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicard-dialect">Niçard Occitan</a>, while Italian was the language of administration. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a> was born there in 1807.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a> from 1792 to 1814. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-turin-1860">Treaty of Turin</a> of 1860, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii">Victor Emmanuel II</a> ceded it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-french-empire">Second French Empire</a> in return for help in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-unification">Italian unification</a>, ratified by a plebiscite.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-nice.jpg" alt="County of Nice" width="320" height="204"><figcaption>Image: Patricia.fidi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_County_of_Nice.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1388 CE – 1860 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nice</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Amadeus VII of Savoy, Emmanuel Philibert of Savoy, Victor Emmanuel II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Occitan and Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nice, Nizza</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1624&amp;focus=county-of-nice" aria-label="County of Nice on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4855 629 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Nice lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5175 885L5140 827M5175 885L5140 827M5175 885L5226 1028M5175 885L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5140 827h0M5140 827h0M5226 1028h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5175 885h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5175 885h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nice. <a href="/atlas?year=1624&amp;focus=county-of-nice">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
